AVE host tests
==============

Run python3 run.py with a C compiler providing ASan and UBSan (CC may name
its executable). No encoder, firmware or captured command image is needed.

run.py reads the real AVE structs and compiles the unmodified bodies of
ave-image.c, ave-layout.c, ave-abi.c, ave-writer.c and ave-cmd.c, plus the real
buffer-allocation,
free, reply and firmware-build-gate functions. Only includes and unused
kernel-facing declarations are omitted. shim.h supplies host primitives;
boundary.h replaces IPC, DMA and logging. This does not validate the kernel
API integration, DART mappings, boot sequence or output extraction.

--compare-baseline PATH builds an older AVE source directory and compares
all bytes of 288 synthetic sessions (1,440 Start/Process commands, including
headers, addresses and zero padding). It covers both codecs, geometry,
profiles, B-frame settings, rates, CBR/VBR and forced-key-frame fields.

--build PATH retains the executable for offline capture QA. Its --case
interface emits synthetic commands; capture inputs and generated artifacts
must stay outside the public source tree. Compare only with the matching
firmware layout, mask enumerated pointer fields and host-only headers, and
report inherited differences explicitly. The 26A428 description is not
reachable through the runtime CRC lookup.

The host shim intentionally uses stdint types, Linux's private ENOTSUPP
value and side-effect-free calls to kernel-like arithmetic macros. Those
produce checkpatch PREFER_KERNEL_TYPES, ENOTSUPP and MACRO_ARG_REUSE notices.
MAINTAINERS already covers the entire AVE directory (FILE_PATH_CHANGES).

The ABI refactor also has in-kernel arm64 KUnit tests selected by
VIDEO_APPLE_AVE_CMD_KUNIT_TEST. The host runner understands both the older
single-builder sources and the per-ABI writer split for baseline comparison.
